Keep the modification time of a cpio hard link as unsigned.
The time of a hard-linked entry is kept in an int for links created at
the end, so a time after 2038 became negative, and cpio -im set a date
in 1901 on an empty hard-linked file. The header field is an unsigned
32-bit number; store it as unsigned.

---
 archival/libarchive/get_header_cpio.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/archival/libarchive/get_header_cpio.c
+++ b/archival/libarchive/get_header_cpio.c
@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@
 	struct hardlinks_t *next;
 	int inode; /* TODO: must match maj/min too! */
 	int mode ;
-	int mtime; /* These three are useful only in corner case */
+	unsigned mtime; /* These three are useful only in corner case */
 	int uid  ; /* of hardlinks with zero size body */
 	int gid  ;
 	char name[1];
